    <DataNode elementId="AT4G37870-MONOMER" textLabel="phosphoenolpyruvate carboxykinase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9T074" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="575" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">PCK1 is a cytosolic enzyme that has phosphoenolpyruvate carboxykinase (PEPCK) activity. The function of this enzyme was demonstrated through a reduction in PEPCK activity observed in the leaf veins of a &lt;i&gt;pck1-2&lt;/i&gt; mutant |CITS: [19807880]|. This suggests that although there is a |FRAME:AT5G65690-MONOMER PEPCK2| (PCK2) ortholog of this enzyme in |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col|, PCK1 is likely to provide the majority of the PEPCK activity present in leaf veins |CITS: [19807880]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G37870-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT4G37870.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR30031" />
