    <DataNode elementId="AT1G79750-MONOMER" textLabel="NADP-dependent malic enzyme 4, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9CA83" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="735" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The NADP-ME4 enzyme catalyzes the NADP+- dependent oxidative decarboxylation of |FRAME: MAL| leading to the formation of |FRAME: PYRUVATE| |CITS:[16113210][18288573]|. It can also act in the reverse direction in a reductive carboxylation reaction. In fact, its activity in this reverse direction was almost 2-fold higher than its activity in the forward direction. This activity was substantially inhibited by malate |CITS:[18288573]|. In addition, NADP-ME4 can also carry out pyruvate reduction and oxaloacetate decarboxylation &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; though these reactions were observed under non-physiological conditions (e.g. pH 5.5) |CITS: [18288573]|. NADP-ME4 can form both dimers and tetramers |CITS: [16113210]|. In a family of four NADP-MEs found in Arabidopsis, it is the only one that localizes to the plastid while the other three appear to be cytosolic |CITS: [16113210][18288573]|. The NADP-ME4 transcript appears to be constitutively expressed based on RT-PCR analyses |CITS: [16113210]|. NADP-ME4 may play a role in providing pyruvate for |FRAME: PYRUVDEHYD-PWY acetyl-CoA production| to serve as an input into |FRAME: PWY-4381| |CITS:[16113210]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G79750-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G79750.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9CA83" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtNADP-ME4" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="NADP-malic enzyme 4" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-7267" />
