    <DataNode elementId="AT5G25880-MONOMER" textLabel="NADP-dependent malic enzyme 3" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9XGZ0" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="815" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The NADP-ME3 enzyme catalyzes the NADP+- dependent oxidative decarboxylation of |FRAME: MAL| leading to the formation of |FRAME: PYRUVATE| |CITS: [19725876][16113210][18288573]|. It can also act in the reverse direction in a reductive carboxylation reaction and can utilize |FRAME: NAD| for the oxidative decarboxylation of |FRAME: MAL|, but with a lower k&lt;sub&gt;cat&lt;/sub&gt; than in the presence of |FRAME: NADP|. In addition, it can also carry out pyruvate reduction and oxaloacetate decarboxylation &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; though these reactions were observed under non-physiological conditions (e.g. pH 5.5) |CITS: [18288573]|. NADP-ME3 can form homooligomers, most likely octamers and/or hexamers |CITS: [16113210]|. It is one of the three cytosolic isoforms in Arabidopsis |CITS: [19725876][16113210][18288573]|. The NADP-ME3 transcript appears to be preferentially expressed in trichomes and pollen |CITS: [16113210]|. In the trichomes, this enzyme may provide reducing power to help with glutathione-mediated detoxification of xenobiotics and cytotoxins |CITS: [16113210]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G25880-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT5G25880.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9XGZ0" />
