    <DataNode elementId="AT2G19900-MONOMER" textLabel="NADP-dependent malic enzyme 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O82191" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="1200" centerY="895" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The NADP-ME1 enzyme catalyzes the NADP+- dependent oxidative decarboxylation of |FRAME: MAL| leading to the formation of |FRAME: PYRUVATE| |CITS:[16113210][18288573]|. It can also act in the reverse direction in a reductive carboxylation reaction. In addition, it can also carry out pyruvate reduction and oxaloacetate decarboxylation &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; though these reactions were observed under non-physiological conditions (e.g. pH 5.5) |CITS: [18288573]|. NADP-ME1 can form homooligomers, most likely octamers and/or hexamers |CITS: [16113210]|. It is also believed to be a cytosolic protein |CITS: [16113210][18288573]|. The NADP-ME1 transcript appears to be preferentially expressed in roots based on RT-PCR analyses. More specifically, promoter:GUS experiments reveal that it is expressed during the late stages of embryogenesis, that during germination, its expression is restricted to the root tip, and in mature plants, it is only detected in some secondary roots |CITS: [16113210]|. This enzyme is notably different from the other NADP-MEs from Arabidopsis based on its catalytic properties. Its exact function &lt;i&gt;in vivo&lt;/i&gt; has not be determined but it may play a role in organic acid cycling and may employ respiratory CO&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; in this process |CITS: [18288573]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G19900-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G19900.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O82191" />
