    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT3G54050-MONOMER" textLabel="fructose 1,6-bisphosphatase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="P25851" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="1055" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">Note: The information concerning this enzyme described below was determined using |FRAME: AT3G54050-MONOMER HCEF1| from |FRAME: ORG4FS-2|. However, there is no strong evidence that sequence of the |FRAME: AT3G54050-MONOMER HCEF1| protein from |FRAME: ORG-5862| is notably different from the protein sequence for |FRAME: ORG-5993|, therefore it seems likely the the proteins will behave in the same manner. |FRAME: AT3G54050-MONOMER HCEF1| is a chloroplastic fructose 1,6-bisphosphatase (FBPase)|CITS: [15028209][16207701][15448173]|. This enzyme likely plays a role in the |FRAME: CALVIN-PWY Calvin-Benson-Bassham cycle| in the stroma of the chloroplast |CITS: [16207701][15448173]|. Although it is not predicted to have a direct role in cytosolic |FRAME: SUCROSE sucrose| formation (which involves the |FRAME: AT1G43670-MONOMER cytosolic FBP|), plants with reduced levels of |FRAME: AT3G54050-MONOMER HCEF1| have increased levels of |FRAME: SUCROSE sucrose|. They also have net higher photosynthetic rates and higher cyclic electron flow |CITS: [20081115][15448173]|, in contrast to plants with reduced |FRAME: AT1G43670-MONOMER cytosolic FBP| that exhibit a reduction in photosynthesis |CITS: [18811733]|. FBPase enzymes typically exist as homotetrameric complexes |CITS: [1849642]|, but this has not yet been experiementally verified for |FRAME: AT3G54050-MONOMER HCEF1|. In addition, these enzymes are typically subject to allosteric inhibition by |FRAME: CPD-535 &amp;beta;-D-fructose 2,6-bisphosphate| and |FRAME: AMP AMP| |CITS:[CSEKE84]|. Although the cytosolic and chloroplastic versions of this protein are structurally quite similar, the chloroplastic isoforms typically have an extra loop of 2030 amino acids that contains three cysteines that are required for the disulfide bridge that allows for light-mediated redox-based regulation of this enzyme |CITS: [10581254]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G54050-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G54050.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="P25851" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="fructose 1,6-bisphosphate 1-phosphatase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="chloroplastic fructose 1,6-bisphosphate phosphatase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="fructose 1,6-bisphosphate phosphatase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_4" value="chloroplastic fructose 1,6-bisphosphatase" />
      <Property key="Synonym_5" value="FBPase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-18732" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G54050.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT3G54050" />
